{# CC-LAB-0132: this shape's sink reads request.getInputStream() directly
   (binary deserialization -- converting to a String first, as raw_body.java.j2
   does for the XML/text-shaped XXE cell, would corrupt binary data). This
   source module intentionally renders no code; it exists to keep this
   emitter's source/sink/complexity composition contract uniform across
   shapes rather than special-casing this one shape into skipping it. #}
        // Declared absent-input behavior (CC-LAB-0244, PA-0053/PA-0054): a
        // request that declares an empty body (Content-Length: 0) is a
        // handled 400 before the sink reads the stream. The stream itself is
        // left unread here (binary data); a chunked empty body still reaches
        // the sink's own handled 400 (EOF).
        if (request.getContentLengthLong() == 0) {
            return com.fuzzlab.trackernest.SiteLayout.missingInput(400, "empty request body");
        }
